;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "fpio - functional programming and IO - Gordon 1994"
 :source "/Users/ryl/SyncMobile/Papers/fpio - functional programming and IO - Gordon 1994.pdf"
 :page 3
 :exercises "A Type 3 TOC page whose leader fills are separate records: the
dots are cmmi periods dvips names \":\" by byte, each served as its
own same-baseline record between the entry's text and its folio.
The fill strips by repetition - whatever the glyph - and the entry
pairs with its folio, one entry per line: the chapter rows (\"4
Operational precongruence 37\") and the math-font fragments (the M
of \"4.3 Ground and confined relations in M\") pair on the page's
own contents evidence, and the first entry pairs inside the top
margin band, where the folio it now closes on would read as a
running head's without the claimed exemption.  No entry promotes
to a synthesized heading.  Captured red for the fills gluing to
the next entry's text (mid-sentence); healed by the leader strip."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
